<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech chemicals firm swings into red in Q1.</title>
<headline>Czech chemicals firm swings into red in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for three month period ending March 31, 1997, according to Czech accounting standards (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit		   -1.08 (loss) vs	64.01</p>
<p> Net profit		     -1.08 (loss) vs	39.04</p>
<p> Operating profit	     27.98	  vs	82.74</p>
<p> Sales of own goods</p>
<p> and services		  692.07	  vs     775.49</p>
<p> Output			  691.44	  vs     755.29</p>
<p> Total assets		4,019.80	  vs   3,270.09</p>
<p> Basic capital	     1,721.03	  vs   1,721.03</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Moravske Chemicke Zavody a.s.. The firm's shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE). Results were provided by the PSE.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
